  "name": "mini-sui",
  "description": "A reference implementation of the Sui Lutris protocol, a hybrid blockchain architecture that bifurcates transaction processing into Byzantine Consistent Broadcast for single-writer owned objects and a sequenced consensus path for shared-access objects. It encapsulates validator state transitions, causal dependency tracking via persistent data structures, and the epoch-based reconfiguration logic defined in the Sui Lutris whitepaper.",
